<title>USA: ValliCorp completes Auburn merger.</title>
<headline>ValliCorp completes Auburn merger.</headline>
<dateline>FRESNO, Calif. 1996-09-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>ValliCorp Holdings Inc said Tuesday it completed its merger with Auburn Bancorp.</p>
<p>Auburn has assets of some $75 million and three branches located in Sacramento, Placer and Nevada Counties in California.</p>
<p>Auburn shareholders will receive 0.8209 shares of ValliCorp common stock for each share of Auburn common stock, resulting in the issuance of approximately 850,000 ValliCorp shares, including 327,000 treasury shares.</p>
<p>The deal is structured as a tax-free exchange and is planned to be accounted for using the purchase method.</p>
</text>
